    {
      "ref": "RFC7517 §7 ¶2",
      "rfc": 7517,
      "section": "Encrypted JWK and Encrypted JWK Set Formats",
      "figure": false,
      "text": "JWK Sets containing non-public key material will also need to be encrypted under these circumstances. The use of an Encrypted JWK Set, which is a JWE with the UTF-8 encoding of a JWK Set as its plaintext value, is recommended for this purpose. The processing of Encrypted JWK Sets is identical to the processing of other JWEs. A \"cty\" (content type) Header Parameter value of \"jwk-set+json\" MUST be used to indicate that the content of the JWE is a JWK Set, unless the application knows that the encrypted content is a JWK Set by another means or convention, in which case the \"cty\" value would typically be omitted."
